Z||000015||Eric||11-29-1999||07:27 PM||||Hey Chadman, I'm in Sunbury.  What kind and color of car do you have so I can watch out for you.  Mine will be black with gold wheels.  I was thinking of joining COFE last year, but I've been trying to restore my 88GT and it has been floating above my garage floor for the past five months.  Maybe next year.  I know Jerry Isbell.  He helped me decide to do a 3.1 rebuild and basically talked me into buying an 88.  <P>What kind of things does the club do?  I'm into racing and having fun with my car not sitting around talking to other people about what kind of paste wax they recommend.  That's why I belong to the Ohio Vally chapter of the SCCA.  They autocross about every other weekend seven months out of the year.  I really enjoy that and I was expecting to see more Fieros there, but there was only myself. I did see a really clean red 85 GT today going South on 71 by Polaris at about 12:00, belong to anyone?||||reg||1
Z||000016||ChadMan||11-30-1999||09:03 AM||||Eric, my 88 Coupe is medium red metallic with factory 14" alloys.  (There's some Asian guy in N.Columbus with an 88 Coupe just like mine but with whitewalls - yuck!)<P>COFE is fun, but it's mainly into country cruising, car shows, and meeting for pizza.  I too would like to get involved in autocrossing next summer.<P>Would anybody be interested in attending the vintage GP weekend at Mid-Ohio next summer?  You see all manner of sports cars there, from the traditional Brit/German/Italian stuff to modern Japanese cars, plus Vettes and a few Fieros.||||reg||14
