Z||000032||william_thorniii||01-13-2000||07:16 PM||||Monkey,<P>You know that you and your medication are always welcome... but you have to have at least one Fiero running by then.  It doesn't have to be capable of making the drive but it has to be running... Just joking of course.  If I keep things going at this rate, I should have at least one to spare.  <P>Ohio Gang,<P>I am always ready and willing.  This weekend is bad for me... The Detriot Auto show opens this weekend, and it has become some what a habit for me.  What about next weekend.  Would Saturday or Sunday be better?  Perhaps we could meet at Mom's (I used to work at Lebanon Nursery and Garden center...back when it was only a field with a wood shack) if we decide on Saturday.  What does everyone think?  <P>William T. Thorn, III<P>I was so excited, because I saw Two GT's today (In Middletown).  One was a maroon/gray 86/87 GT on Central Ave and Manchester and the other was a gold 86 GT heading N. on St. Rt. 73.  I was the guy in the VERY LOUD red/gray 85 GT pulling out of Big Al's Muffler and S. St. Rt. 73 respectively.  ||||reg||10
Z||000033||fiero56||01-13-2000||07:46 PM||||Noooo, not next weekend! I leave for the Detroit auto show on the 20th and won't be back until Sunday. Plus, my Fiero isn't back on the road yet either. Maybe the parts will come in tommorrow. I'm free Saturday the 29th, but not Sunday the 30th.<BR>Plus, Monkey needs a Fiero to drive, and I need to give mine a nice cleaning, it has to be warmer out when we meet... There's so much to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-13-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000034||william_thorniii||01-14-2000||12:40 AM||||56,<P>I guess I more the kind of guy that enjoys action more than words.  Too bad you are going to Motor City next weekend (see my previous post).  I was just thinking that perhaps we should make this a somewhat regular event.  Maybe it is time to re-incarnate a Dayton/Cincinnati area Fiero Club.  Yes I know that Cincinnati still has one of around 20 members, but I think that we could have that many from the Dayton and surrounding areas also.  I realize that I am getting ahead of myself, but I don't want to have to spend hours on the Fiero before we all get to meet.  If that is the case, I will not be able to pencil you all in for the next 5 years or so until I get my project done.  We all have Fiero's and should be proud of what they are the way that they are.  If you watch a car guy closely you will see him often looking, thinking... "what if I were to add fiberglass there and smooth that line?  I wonder what those lights would look like on my car?..."  I am convinced that none of my cars will ever be done.  They will always be in some form of a working state.  So be happy with what you have... Monkey that means to drive your wife's car with the fake cowl induction.  It is all just to have fun.  But next weekend is a no-go.  Everyone let's keep on this and actually get to planning something soon.  <P>William T. Thorn, III  <P>W||||reg||13
Z||000035||Monkeyman||01-14-2000||04:00 AM||||If I'm gonna have a chance of being there, we need to schedule something in advance.  My wife never knows when she's gonna have to work and if we had some notice, she could make some arrangements (she manages a motel).  William-my '86 <B> is </B> running.  Sorta.  I've been driving it back and forth to work for a week now.  It runs rough and the interior is still half done (well...2% finished is more like it <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">), but it's on the road.  I'd spend some money on it, but I want to save the cash for my '85 GT.  That has a lot more potential.||||reg||1
Z||000036||ChadMan||01-14-2000||10:06 AM||||I'd be up for a Fiero get-together just about anywhere within 2 hrs of Columbus (and I might go all the way to Indy if we're going to ride the tour bus around the track - no matter how many times I do that, I want to do it again).  But those of us with wives would definitely need advance notice!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The Sprint Vintage Grand Prix takes place Sunday, June 25, 2000.  We'd need to submit a list of names and cars to their PR guy about two weeks before the event.  Then we could rendezvous somewhere near the track and drive in together.  They set up specially-marked corrals for each car club, so we'd all park together.  Then, during the lunch break, we get to take two parade laps around the track.  It would be fantastic if we could show up with at least five good-looking, good-running Fieros!||||reg||1
